.TH "WINDOW.REQUESTRESIZE" "3JS" "July 17, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Window.requestResize \- Window: requestResize() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]requestResize()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]Window\f[R]
interface updates the size information shared by an embedded document
with its embedding parent, but only if the embedded document has opted
in to sharing its size information via the
\f[CR]<meta name=\(dqresponsive\-embedded\-sizing\(dq>\f[R] meta tag.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
requestResize()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]requestResize()\f[R] method was called from a top\-level
(non\-embedded) document.
.IP \(bu 2
The embedding element is not an \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The embedded document has not opted in to sharing its layout size by
including a \f[CR]<meta name=\(dqresponsive\-embedded\-sizing\(dq>\f[R]
tag.
.RE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] If the parent document doesn\(cqt set the
\f[CR]frame\-sizing\f[R] CSS property on the embedding
\f[CR]<iframe>\f[R], no exception is thrown, but the \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R]
will not be resized.
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
For security and privacy reasons, \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] elements do not by
default expose any information to the parent document about the size of
the content in the document they are embedding.
.PP
To enable responsive sizing of \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] elements based on
their content, the
\f[CR]<meta name=\(dqresponsive\-embedded\-sizing\(dq>\f[R] tag can be
included in an embedded document to opt it in to sharing its size
information with the parent document.
The \f[CR]frame\-sizing\f[R] CSS property can then be set on the
\f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] to cause it to adopt the same horizontal or vertical
size as the embedded document\(cqs actual layout size (termed the
\f[B]internal layout intrinsic size\f[R] in the spec).
This ensures that the document content fits seamlessly into its
embedding \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R], avoiding unnecessary scrollbars.
.PP
The embedded document\(cqs layout size is automatically reported once
when its \f[CR]DOMContentLoaded\f[R] event fires, and again when the
\f[CR]Window\f[R] object\(cqs \f[CR]load\f[R] event fires.
.PP
In other circumstances, you can call the
\f[CR]Window.requestResize()\f[R] method from the embedded document to
make it report an updated layout size; this is typically done from
within the event handler that caused the embedded content to change
size.
If the \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] is sized using \f[CR]frame\-sizing\f[R], it
will then update its size automatically so that it still neatly contains
the embedded content.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using \f[CR]requestResize()\f[R]
This example shows how the \f[CR]requestResize()\f[R] method can be used
to automatically resize an \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] when the layout size of
its embedded document content changes.
.PP
We have two documents, the main \f[CR]index.html\f[R] document, and the
embedded \f[CR]frame.html\f[R] document.
.SS The main \f[CR]index.html\f[R]
The \f[CR]index.html\f[R] document\(cqs HTML contains a heading and an
\f[CR]<iframe>\f[R], into which is embedded the \f[CR]frame.html\f[R]
document:
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]h1\f[R]>Responsive iframes \(em basic example</\f[B]h1\f[R]>

<\f[B]iframe\f[R] src=\(dqframe.html\(dq></\f[B]iframe\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
In the \f[CR]index.html\f[R] CSS, we give the \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] a
\f[CR]frame\-sizing\f[R] value of \f[CR]content\-block\-size\f[R].
Because the \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] has a horizontal
\f[CR]writing\-mode\f[R], its \f[CR]height\f[R] will be set to the
embedded document\(cqs layout height.
.IP
.EX
iframe {
  frame\-sizing: content\-block\-size;
  \f[B]border\f[R]: 2px solid gray;
}
.EE
.SS The embedded \f[CR]frame.html\f[R]
The \f[CR]frame.html\f[R] document includes a \f[CR]<div>\f[R] element
with a \f[CR]tabindex\f[R] value of \f[CR]0\f[R] set so that it is
focusable.
It contains a heading and some paragraphs.
The document also includes the
\f[CR]<meta name=\(dqresponsive\-embedded\-sizing\(dq />\f[R] tag, which
opts it in to sharing its content layout size with the parent document.
Finally, we include a \f[CR]<script>\f[R] element containing some
JavaScript to control the demo.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]head\f[R]>
  ...

  <\f[B]meta\f[R] name=\(dqresponsive\-embedded\-sizing\(dq />

  ...
</\f[B]head\f[R]>
<\f[B]body\f[R]>
  <\f[B]div\f[R] tabindex=\(dq0\(dq>
    <\f[B]h1\f[R]>This is my frame</\f[B]h1\f[R]>
    <\f[B]p\f[R]>This is the content of my discontent.</\f[B]p\f[R]>
    <\f[B]p\f[R]>This is some more content.</\f[B]p\f[R]>
  </\f[B]div\f[R]>
  <\f[B]script\f[R]>
    ...
  </\f[B]script\f[R]>
</\f[B]body\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
The script inside \f[CR]frame.html\f[R] starts by grabbing a reference
to the \f[CR]<div>\f[R] element.
It then sets \f[CR]click\f[R] and \f[CR]keydown\f[R] event listeners on
the \f[CR]<div>\f[R], both of which run a custom function called
\f[CR]addParagraph()\f[R] when the event fires.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] divElem = document.querySelector(\(dqdiv\(dq);
divElem.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, addParagraph);
window.addEventListener(\(dqkeydown\(dq, addParagraph);
.EE
.PP
The \f[CR]addParagraph()\f[R] function generates a new paragraph element
and appends it to the end of the \f[CR]<div>\f[R] as a child, increasing
its height.
It then calls \f[CR]requestResize()\f[R] so that the new size is
reported to the parent document.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] addParagraph() {
  \f[B]const\f[R] para = document.createElement(\(dqp\(dq);
  para.textContent = \(dqNew content.\(dq;
  divElem.appendChild(para);
  window.requestResize();
}
.EE
.SS Result
Open our \c
.UR https://mdn.github.io/dom-examples/responsive-iframe-sizing/js-request-resize/
\f[CR]requestResize()\f[R] demo
.UE \c
\ in a separate tab to see it in action (\c
.UR https://github.com/mdn/dom-examples/tree/main/responsive-iframe-sizing/js-request-resize
see the source code
.UE \c
).
.PP
Even though no explicit \f[CR]height\f[R] has been set on the
\f[CR]<iframe>\f[R], it is sized to the right height to exactly contain
its embedded document, with no scroll bars.
Try clicking on the content or focusing it and pressing a key on the
keyboard.
As a new paragraph is added to the \f[CR]<div>\f[R], the
\f[CR]<div>\f[R] grows in height, but the \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R] also grows
in height to match it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]frame\-sizing\f[R] CSS property
.IP \(bu 2
CSS box sizing module
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]<meta name=\(dqresponsive\-embedded\-sizing\(dq>\f[R]
